y optional, never a standing deliverable\",\"done\":true}]\nnotes:spawn queued: [implementer] developer (codex) (run=RUN-260720-bc3052, max_parallel=20)\\nspawn run started: [implementer] developer (codex) (run=RUN-260720-bc3052)\\nImplemented the accepted schema-6 core/security contract from the verified 6308d99d... input on a clean branch rooted at required origin/main 57c1f568.... Decision and threat-boundary findings are recorded in decisions/0004 and TASK-260720-1nvomm_results.md. This is a documentation-only owned scope: schemas/vectors/tests are downstream-owned and were not edited; existing validation passed. The host Python initially lacked jsonschema, so validation used a task-local venv populated from pinned requirements-dev.txt.\\nagent completed: [implementer] developer (codex) (exit=0)\\nspawn run completed: codex (run=RUN-260720-bc3052, pid=1744, exit=0)\\nspawn queued: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (run=RUN-260720-9fca47, max_parallel=20)\\nspawn run started: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (run=RUN-260720-9fca47)\\nReview verdict: changes requested. protocol/core.md weakens two accepted MUST-level details: bootstrap probes do not explicitly use a manager-owned empty CWD with GOENV=off and GOTOOLCHAIN=local in the bootstrap environment, and go-list trust does not require the accepted Standard && Goroot conjunction. Full evidence and green validation results are in TASK-260720-1nvomm_review-verdict.md. Route to documentation rework, then a new reviewer cycle.\\nagent completed: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (exit=0)\\nspawn run completed: codex (run=RUN-260720-9fca47, pid=16192, exit=0)\\nspawn queued: [implementer] developer (codex) (run=RUN-260720-d7e0fe, max_parallel=20)\\nspawn run started: [implementer] developer (codex) (run=RUN-260720-d7e0fe)\\nReviewer rework applied in protocol/core.md: bootstrap probes now use a manager-owned empty CWD with private roots, GOENV=off, GOTOOLCHAIN=local, normalized locale, and no inherited GOROOT/target; go-list toolchain trust now requires Standard == true and Goroot == true. Scoped validator and full make validate pass in the pinned task-local venv; git diff --check passes. Updated TASK-260720-1nvomm_results.md and TASK-260720-1nvomm_validation.log with exact evidence.\\nagent completed: [implementer] developer (codex) (exit=0)\\nspawn completion blocked: no new task-scoped outcome artifact was attached. Add an outcome resource named like TASK-260720-1nvomm_results.md and then set status back to to-review.\\nspawn run completed: codex (run=RUN-260720-d7e0fe, pid=24410, exit=0)\\nOrchestrator recovery: content rework is complete and validated, but RUN-260720-d7e0fe could not hand off because it updated existing outcome resources instead of attaching a distinct new task-scoped rework outcome. Add a new TASK-260720-1nvomm_rework-1.md outcome resource containing the two corrections and exact validation evidence; do not change project files unless evidence is inaccurate; then route to to-review.\\nspawn queued: [implementer] developer (codex) (run=RUN-260720-b95c7d, max_parallel=20)\\nspawn run started: [implementer] developer (codex) (run=RUN-260720-b95c7d)\\nRecovery audit confirmed both reviewer-requested MUST-level corrections and found one additional accepted-contract gap: dependency command narrowing still said script-only. protocol/core.md now permits schema-6 build commands while explicitly retaining script-only behavior for schemas 1 through 5. Evidence is attached as TASK-260720-1nvomm_rework-1.md; scoped and combined validation gates pass.\\nagent completed: [implementer] developer (codex) (exit=0)\\nspawn run completed: codex (run=RUN-260720-b95c7d, pid=37242, exit=0)\\nspawn queued: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (run=RUN-260720-e7562d, max_parallel=20)\\nspawn run started: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (run=RUN-260720-e7562d)\\nFinal review verdict: accepted. All acceptance criteria and accepted-contract decisions are covered in the three owned documents; prior MUST-level gaps and legacy dependency narrowing are corrected. Independent scoped and full validation gates pass. Evidence attached as TASK-260720-1nvomm_review-2.md.\\nagent completed: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (exit=0)\\nspawn run completed: codex (run=RUN-260720-e7562d, pid=43454, exit=0)\\nScope delta requested 2026-07-27: add first-class external build-repository dependencies for Go CLI commands, with later closed drivers for other languages. This is a genuine architecture decision, not settled board decomposition. Produce an architecture-only decision packet; do not edit product, spec, schema, code, tests, release metadata, or existing decision documents. Resolve: (1) manifest schema shape for a named external Git build repository and immutable revision/lock semantics; (2) repository-root descriptor name, schema version, target selection, monorepo build_root/source_dir rules, and backward compatibility; (3) exact access behavior: syntax-only offline warning, install/audit hard failure when inaccessible, credential ownership, allowed Git transports, local operator substitutions, moved refs, submodules, LFS, symlinks and special files; (4) snapshot and audit equivalence to in-skill source, including compiler-visible root, dependency graph containment, source identity, receipts, marker v2 and protected cache; (5) deterministic build, install, PATH/shim verification and rollback; (6) platform-owned signing policy and the boundary between local signing and release-time notarization; (7) the extension rule for future Rust, Swift, Kotlin/JVM, C/C++, .NET and other closed drivers; (8) exact impact on existing spec, Curator, cocoaskills and interoperability tasks, while Linux remains a separate later native validation. Explicitly reconcile the user proposal that the repository descriptor name the final binary and output location with the accepted protocol rule forbidding package-controlled executable names and output selection. Prefer logical target IDs plus manager-derived command name and private staging path unless evidence supports another closed design. Audit must happen before any compiler execution. Repository access failure must warn during offline/static check when verification cannot be attempted and must fail install before mutation when source cannot be resolved. Credentials and signing identities must never come from the package descriptor. Research authoritative Git, Go build, platform signing/notarization and sandbox constraints as needed. Persist the decision and threat model as a new task-scoped outcome resource, include concrete JSON examples and normative MUST/MUST NOT recommendations, record source links, then route to to-review for an independent architecture review.\\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: codex via explicit_override\\nspawn launch composition: degraded_contract_unavailable; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=codex; schema=1; diagnostic=composition_contract_unavailable; bare child launch retained\\nspawn queued: [analyst] solution-architect (codex) (run=RUN-260727-482663, max_parallel=20)\\nspawn run started: [analyst] solution-architect (codex) (run=RUN-260727-482663)\\nArchitecture logbook 2026-07-27 — resolved the external build-repository scope delta without editing project/spec files. Recommendation: freeze schema 6/go-v1; add schema 7, strict build_repositories, locked Git commit with optional tag assertion, curator-build.json schema 1 logical targets, new closed go-repository-v1, receipt v2, marker v3, and claim v3/rc.5. Repository targets cannot select executable names, output paths, argv, environment, credentials, signing, hooks, or plugins; manifest command keys and manager-private staging remain authoritative. Exact external snapshots must be raw-tree validated and independently audited before cache lookup/compiler on real, cache-hit, dry-run, install/repair/audit paths; syntax-only offline checks warn when verification is unavailable, while mutating/coverage-claiming operations fail before mutation. Git submodules, LFS hydration, links/special modes, checkout filters, package credential helpers, and package signing identities are rejected. Local substitutions stay operator-owned in Skillfile.dev v2; release notarization/AuthentiCode stays outside install-time builds; Linux remains separate native validation. Outcome TASK-260720-1nvomm_external-build-repositories-architecture.md attached at SHA-256 969de48ae9230e6696c2c5423c3d71d966ba66626c6cbd2e5d77d9a78cb6352c; 4 JSON examples parsed and required-topic audit passed.\\nValidation anomaly 2026-07-27 — task-board validate reports 45 pre-existing board-wide issues outside this architecture scope: legacy broken dependency text, parent-status mismatches, two orphan resource files, and an unsupported STORY-260720-35dck7 container link. The new TASK-260720-1nvomm outcome resource is referenced correctly and byte-identical to the validated source artifact. No unrelated board records were modified.\\nagent completed: [analyst] solution-architect (codex) (exit=0)\\nspawn run completed: codex (run=RUN-260727-482663, pid=31641, exit=0)\\nIndependent architecture review directive 2026-07-27: review TASK-260720-1nvomm_external-build-repositories-architecture.md as an adversarial protocol/security reviewer. Do not edit product/spec/code or the producer resource. Verify preservation of schema 1-6 and go-v1 semantics; schema 7/versioning justification; exact immutable Git lock and object-format behavior; URL, remote-helper, credential, config, hook/filter/LFS/submodule and raw-object extraction boundaries; offline warning versus install/audit hard-error semantics including protected cached snapshots; descriptor monorepo path semantics and compiler-visible containment; whether whole-repository audit/source identity is necessary and operationally coherent; audit-before-cache/compiler ordering; receipt v2, marker v3, cache currentness, deduplication, rollback and structural PATH/shim checks; signing/notarization boundary on macOS and Windows; future-driver extension rules; and precise mapping to existing board work without premature implementation. Explicitly challenge the rejection of repository-controlled binary names/output paths and confirm that logical targets plus manifest command keys satisfy the stated requirement without reopening output selection. Check JSON examples and cited primary sources. Attach a new task-scoped review verdict resource. If accepted, set done; if changes are required, list exact defects and route to analysis. Do not create or edit implementation tasks; board refinement remains the parent orchestrator responsibility.\\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: codex via explicit_override\\nspawn launch composition: degraded_contract_unavailable; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=codex; schema=1; diagnostic=composition_contract_unavailable; bare child launch retained\\nspawn queued: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (run=RUN-260727-232f26, max_parallel=20)\\nspawn run started: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (run=RUN-260727-232f26)\\nIndependent external-build-repository architecture verdict: changes requested. High-level schema-7/new-driver/output/audit/signing design is sound, but receipt/cache identity does not bind effective substitutions or mixed local/external schema-7 builds; raw Git extraction does not close replace-ref, lazy-fetch, alternate/promisor, and ambient-config indirection; canonical URL/SSH/tag grammar is underspecified; and status/protected-snapshot currentness is omitted. Exact evidence and primary sources are attached in TASK-260720-1nvomm_external-build-repositories-review.md. Route to analysis, then a new reviewer cycle.\\nagent completed: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (exit=0)\\nspawn run completed: codex (run=RUN-260727-232f26, pid=50429, exit=0)\\nArchitecture rework directive 2026-07-27: consume the independent verdict TASK-260720-1nvomm_external-build-repositories-review.md and produce a new complete superseding packet TASK-260720-1nvomm_external-build-repositories-architecture-v2.md. Do not edit product/spec/code or overwrite either prior resource. Close every required finding normatively: bind both declared and effective source identity, object format, full effective commit, substitution flag/type and external digest into receipt-v2/cache identity; define mixed schema-7 local go-v1 plus external go-repository-v1 receipt/marker-v3 behavior; define a clean manager-owned Git child environment and process graph that disables replacement refs and lazy fetch, rejects alternates, grafts and promisor/partial-clone state, prevents ambient config/rewrite/proxy/SSH/helper/filter/hook influence, and proves complete local object availability before audit; precisely reuse/narrow canonical source identity for HTTPS/SSH including userinfo, username, port, host case, .git and SCP forms; define operator-owned SSH host verification and exact safe tag/ref grammar; add read-only status currentness behavior, repair behavior, and marker/journal GC roots for snapshot and artifact caches. Preserve accepted portions, concrete JSON examples, signing boundary, future-driver rules and Linux-later validation. Validate examples and cite primary sources. Attach the new v2 resource and route to to-review for a fresh independent reviewer.\\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: codex via explicit_override\\nspawn launch composition: degraded_contract_unavailable; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=codex; schema=1; diagnostic=composition_contract_unavailable; bare child launch retained\\nspawn queued: [analyst] solution-architect (codex) (run=RUN-260727-c577a5, max_parallel=20)\\nspawn run started: [analyst] solution-architect (codex) (run=RUN-260727-c577a5)\ncreated:2026-07-20T01:44:31Z\nupdated:2026-07-27T18:16:30Z\nisBlocked:false\nisAdvisoryBlocked:false\nchildren:[]\npreconditionResources:[{\"name\":\"TASK-260720-1nvomm_artifact-map.puml\",\"uri\":\"file://TASK-260720-1nvomm/TASK-260720-1nvomm_artifact-map.puml\",\"description\":\"Implementation planning diagram showing normative contract ownership and downstream consumers\"},{\"name\":\"TASK-260720-1nvomm_accepted-contract.md\",\"uri\":\"file://TASK-260720-1nvomm/TASK-260720-1nvomm_accepted-contract.md\",\"description\":\"Accepted compile-only driver contract, verified at SHA-256 6308d99d8bdad4445841bc1cbd230cadbed0020012d0e9d38d877b413348f681\"}]\noutcomeResources:[{\"name\":\"TASK-260720-1nvomm_artifact-map.svg\",\"uri\":\"file://TASK-260720-1nvomm/TASK-260720-1nvomm_artifact-map.svg\",\"description\":\"Rendered artifact ownership diagram linked to the normative contract task\"},{\"name\":\"TASK-260720-1nvomm_spawn-log_-implementer--developer--codex-.log\",\"uri\":\"file://TASK-260720-1nvomm/TASK-260720-1nvomm_spawn-log_-implementer--developer--codex-.log\",\"description\":\"System spawn log captured by task-board\"},{\"name\":\"TASK-260720-1nvomm_results.md\",\"uri\":\"file://TASK-260720-1nvomm/TASK-260720-1nvomm_results.md\",\"description\":\"Implementation scope, complete accepted-decision mapping, reviewer rework, exclusion proof, and verification results\"},{\"name\":\"TASK-260720-1nvomm_validation.log\",\"uri\":\"file://TASK-260720-1nvomm/TASK-260720-1nvomm_validation.log\",\"description\":\"Passing scoped and full validation output after reviewer-requested core corrections\"},{\"name\":\"TASK-260720-1nvomm_spawn-log_-reviewer--reviewer--codex-.log\",\"uri\":\"file://TASK-260720-1nvomm/TASK-260720-1nvomm_spawn-log_-reviewer--reviewer--codex-.log\",\"description\":\"System spawn log captured by task-board\"},{\"name\":\"TASK-260720-1nvomm_review-verdict.md\",\"uri\":\"file://TASK-260720-1nvomm/TASK-260720-1nvomm_review-verdict.md\",\"description\":\"Reviewer verdict, contract gaps, and validation evidence\"},{\"name\":\"TASK-260720-1nvomm_rework-1.md\",\"uri\":\"file://TASK-260720-1nvomm/TASK-260720-1nvomm_rework-1.md\",\"description\":\"Reviewer rework co